WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:06.733
Allow me to explain the rules.

01:08.359 --> 01:11.696
Here's the game we are about to play.

01:11.780 --> 01:14.407
Difficulty level, Queen of Hearts,

01:14.491 --> 01:15.742
"Croquet."

01:16.534 --> 01:17.786
"Croquet"?

01:18.536 --> 01:20.663
Often called lawn billiards,

01:20.747 --> 01:23.833
it's a ball game that was popularized
in 19th century England.

01:24.584 --> 01:28.338
But I'm afraid
it's not very well-known in Japan.

01:29.631 --> 01:30.882
I don't know the rules.

01:32.133 --> 01:34.886
It's perfectly fine if you don't know
how to play croquet properly.

01:35.929 --> 01:36.846
You see,

01:38.181 --> 01:40.266
it doesn't matter if you win or lose.

01:41.434 --> 01:42.310
What?

01:43.686 --> 01:45.438
To clear this game,

01:45.939 --> 01:50.360
you simply need to play
three rounds of croquet without quitting.

01:51.194 --> 01:54.030
If you quit before we're done,
it's game over.

01:54.114 --> 01:55.949
You can even have weapons.

01:56.908 --> 02:01.329
The only rule is
to complete three rounds of croquet.

02:05.250 --> 02:09.671
If we play until the end,
we clear the game even if we don't win?

02:10.463 --> 02:12.715
That's right. Easy, isn't it?

02:15.218 --> 02:17.720
Now, let's enjoy ourselves.

03:34.297 --> 03:38.426
The game is played with
a wooden mallet and two balls.

03:38.509 --> 03:42.722
You must hit both balls
through six hoops in a prearranged order

03:42.805 --> 03:46.643
and then hit the finishing peg
before the other player to win.

04:15.880 --> 04:16.881
Yes!

04:23.972 --> 04:26.975
Round 1, I won.

04:30.395 --> 04:33.231
If we play three full rounds
without quitting, we clear the game

04:34.649 --> 04:35.900
and we win.

04:37.402 --> 04:38.569
Just two more rounds.

04:40.154 --> 04:41.656
What in the world is she thinking?

04:47.120 --> 04:49.622
Okay, now for Round 2.

05:10.810 --> 05:14.981
She's simply dragging the game out.

05:16.232 --> 05:18.067
She's just entertaining herself.

05:18.651 --> 05:19.986
We need to finish this game fast.

05:38.421 --> 05:40.590
Oh, my! This is such fun!

05:44.427 --> 05:45.344
Nice!

05:47.180 --> 05:49.182
This is never going to end.

06:09.994 --> 06:11.162
Yes!

06:44.028 --> 06:44.862
I won.

06:50.243 --> 06:52.578
Looks like I lost Round 2.

06:53.538 --> 06:55.456
You've got talent for this.

06:56.499 --> 06:58.668
Okay, let's play Round 3.

07:00.878 --> 07:02.547
I'm feeling a bit weary.

07:03.589 --> 07:05.466
Why don't we have some tea?

07:06.300 --> 07:07.301
Tea?

07:17.228 --> 07:18.354
Forget the tea.

07:18.855 --> 07:19.981
Let's hurry up and play.

07:20.606 --> 07:25.278
Enjoying tea during a match is
proper etiquette for ladies and gentlemen.

07:25.862 --> 07:28.614
Please, enjoy your tea.

07:42.044 --> 07:45.882
When this game is over,
can we go back to the real world?

07:47.884 --> 07:49.594
You'll know when it's over.

07:51.679 --> 07:53.264
Don't ask her any more questions.

07:54.474 --> 07:56.309
Don't listen to what she says.

07:56.392 --> 08:00.146
Just finish this game.
That's all we need to do.

08:01.189 --> 08:03.024
Do you want to know the answer that badly?

08:07.528 --> 08:11.073
My friends died
without knowing the answer.

08:13.659 --> 08:16.496
I want to know the answer
for their sake as well.

08:18.039 --> 08:19.290
That's why I've come this far.

08:19.373 --> 08:23.211
And you want to return to the real world.

08:25.671 --> 08:26.923
Can we?

08:29.842 --> 08:30.760
Who knows?

08:32.053 --> 08:33.971
I certainly can't tell you that.

08:37.517 --> 08:42.230
Besides, this just might be
the ruins of that other world.

08:43.523 --> 08:44.690
You talk like that,

08:45.483 --> 08:47.527
but I bet you don't even know
the answer yourself.

08:48.819 --> 08:49.904
I do know.

08:57.370 --> 08:59.121
I guess I have no choice.

09:01.123 --> 09:02.792
If you want to know that badly,

09:04.168 --> 09:05.503
I'll just have to tell you

09:07.046 --> 09:08.756
the truth about this land.

09:17.306 --> 09:20.893
However, you must accept that
no matter what I tell you,

09:22.228 --> 09:24.897
it was you who wanted to hear it.

09:26.857 --> 09:28.276
Don't you forget that.

09:35.032 --> 09:37.702
Have you sometimes wondered

09:37.785 --> 09:40.246
what the world
would be like in the future?

09:40.955 --> 09:42.123
In the future?

09:42.206 --> 09:43.082
Yes.

09:43.583 --> 09:46.460
Nanotechnology, renewable energy,

09:46.544 --> 09:51.048
iPS cells, virtual reality,
cryonics, terraforming…

09:52.717 --> 09:58.472
The technology of your era is
still filled with hopes and fantasies.

10:01.058 --> 10:02.476
You should probably be happy.

10:02.977 --> 10:06.188
All those things became a reality.

10:06.689 --> 10:11.611
In fact, technology achieved
radical developments and advances.

10:12.445 --> 10:15.740
In 30 years, the economies
of developing countries will grow,

10:15.823 --> 10:19.076
and the barriers to improving
living standards will be demolished.

10:19.827 --> 10:24.498
In 50 years, lives will be prolonged
thanks to genetic manipulation.

10:26.042 --> 10:27.043
Hold on.

10:28.628 --> 10:30.046
What's this all about?

10:32.673 --> 10:33.883
Don't you understand?

10:35.259 --> 10:37.762
I'm simply telling you

10:40.014 --> 10:43.684
what the future will be like
1,000 years from now.

10:46.520 --> 10:47.438
A thousand years?

10:48.731 --> 10:49.815
In the future?

10:51.400 --> 10:54.737
Since the human race obtained
even greater mental capacity,

10:54.820 --> 10:58.699
perpetual discoveries will be made
in every field of knowledge.

10:59.200 --> 11:04.997
Ten years after the present, that is,
the time you believe you live in,

11:05.665 --> 11:07.875
avatars and virtual reality

11:07.958 --> 11:10.961
will become the way that life is lived,
including how we work and have fun.

11:11.629 --> 11:13.798
In 50 years,
genetic engineering will be used

11:13.881 --> 11:17.301
to treat all diseases,
such as cancer and dementia.

11:17.385 --> 11:18.677
In 100 years,

11:18.761 --> 11:22.264
due to the development of weather control
and other environmental regulating tech,

11:22.348 --> 11:23.933
natural disasters will be eliminated.

11:24.016 --> 11:24.934
In 200 years,

11:25.017 --> 11:27.561
due to a perfect understanding
of brain mechanisms,

11:27.645 --> 11:30.064
it will be possible
to transfer memories and consciousness.

11:30.147 --> 11:31.399
In 300 years,

11:31.482 --> 11:34.026
humans will no longer die
from natural causes

11:34.110 --> 11:36.237
and we will live an average of 300 years.

11:36.320 --> 11:37.655
In 400 years,

11:37.738 --> 11:41.033
due to a perfect understanding of physics,
we'll understand all laws of causality

11:41.117 --> 11:46.122
and be able to scientifically explain
even things such as coincidence and fate.

11:46.872 --> 11:50.459
In 500 years,
nothing unexpected will ever happen.

11:51.043 --> 11:54.463
By achieving
perfect control over everything,

11:54.547 --> 11:56.298
humanity will become nearly immortal.

11:58.217 --> 11:59.552
For the next 500 years,

11:59.635 --> 12:02.888
we'll be able to live
just by injecting pleasure compounds.

12:02.972 --> 12:05.933
That is what the world will be like
1,000 years in the future.

13:05.034 --> 13:10.372
In fact, right now, you are playing
this game in virtual reality.

13:10.873 --> 13:13.876
You're in a deep sleep,
so you've forgotten that.

13:14.752 --> 13:17.254
This kind of game tourism
is the most popular activity

13:17.338 --> 13:19.256
a thousand years in the future.

13:20.299 --> 13:25.471
Since we have become nearly immortal,
we have little reason to live.

13:26.305 --> 13:27.723
The era of 1,000 years earlier,

13:27.806 --> 13:31.602
where the threats of death
and the end of the world were a reality,

13:32.311 --> 13:34.480
has captured our fascination.

13:40.069 --> 13:44.073
Incidentally,
I am the administrator of this system.

13:52.414 --> 13:55.167
Just kidding! I lied about all that.

13:56.460 --> 13:57.336
What?

13:59.004 --> 14:00.256
Cut the crap!

14:03.008 --> 14:04.093
The truth is…

14:06.220 --> 14:07.805
due to genetic manipulation,

14:07.888 --> 14:10.808
massive amounts
of mutant vegetation appeared.

14:11.850 --> 14:13.936
You saw it too, right?

14:14.645 --> 14:18.941
The city has become overrun
with vegetation.

14:20.985 --> 14:25.489
The city became surrounded by mountains.

14:30.953 --> 14:34.373
It was aliens that brought this about.

14:36.542 --> 14:37.459
Aliens?

14:37.960 --> 14:41.088
They captured all of humanity
and wiped out our memories,

14:41.171 --> 14:45.759
and forced us to play all these games
to conduct behavioral experiments on us.

14:47.553 --> 14:50.806
Is that the truth?

14:52.766 --> 14:54.268
Yes, it's the truth.

14:55.686 --> 14:56.645
But…

14:57.688 --> 15:02.985
there is this rumor circulating among
the humans forced to play these games.

15:04.194 --> 15:07.448
In actuality, due to a nuclear war,

15:08.157 --> 15:10.659
humans can no longer live
on the Earth's surface.

15:10.743 --> 15:12.661
Now, the ultra-wealthy,
who live underground,

15:13.495 --> 15:15.664
have put androids
implanted with artificial memories

15:15.748 --> 15:20.836
on the surface to play games,
and are betting on which will survive.

15:36.852 --> 15:38.270
You believe

15:38.354 --> 15:43.859
that you're oppressed humans who are
being forced to play games by aliens.

15:43.943 --> 15:45.194
But the truth is

15:46.862 --> 15:50.783
you're nothing more than androids
that have been implanted

15:51.575 --> 15:53.410
with artificial memories.

15:55.746 --> 15:56.914
And that's the truth?

15:59.583 --> 16:01.335
Just kidding.

16:02.503 --> 16:04.088
We just need to finish one more round.

16:05.005 --> 16:06.590
Stop listening to Mira.

16:07.716 --> 16:10.135
I bet you don't even know the truth.

16:13.138 --> 16:14.640
Maybe so.

16:17.726 --> 16:19.728
Is the truth really that important?

16:22.398 --> 16:25.651
You want to know
for the sake of your deceased friends?

16:32.032 --> 16:33.867
You poor thing.

16:35.369 --> 16:38.205
I can see that your deceased friends

16:38.789 --> 16:42.209
were very, very precious to you,
weren't they?

16:47.798 --> 16:52.428
Incidentally,
I made the Seven of Hearts game.

16:53.929 --> 16:56.932
I mean, you were so close, I just had to.

16:59.727 --> 17:00.769
Arisu!

17:00.853 --> 17:02.104
It's all right.

17:02.604 --> 17:04.023
Please don't stop him.

17:05.315 --> 17:09.903
Having something to hate
is one of the greatest motivators in life.

17:34.970 --> 17:37.097
This is also part of your plan, isn't it?

17:43.228 --> 17:44.646
To have yourself killed

17:45.522 --> 17:47.107
while the game's still going on.

17:49.359 --> 17:51.528
If I kill you in this game,

17:52.112 --> 17:56.950
I won't be able to clear the game
and there will be no game over for me.

17:57.826 --> 18:01.997
In other words,
this game will continue forever.

18:03.499 --> 18:04.500
If that happens,

18:05.626 --> 18:09.379
then all the players in this land
will just wait until their visas run out.

18:12.174 --> 18:13.175
That's exactly

18:14.468 --> 18:19.264
the kind of extreme despair
that you wanted to thrust on us.

18:26.897 --> 18:30.567
While you were playing the games,

18:31.860 --> 18:34.947
didn't you also lose all interest
in what happens in the world?

18:36.448 --> 18:39.952
Did you care about how the world works,
or what its grand purpose is?

18:40.953 --> 18:44.206
Did you care about any of that?

18:45.958 --> 18:48.210
Those things
didn't matter anymore, did they?

18:51.547 --> 18:55.968
Then why does it even matter
what the real truth is?

18:57.261 --> 19:00.430
Arisu, don't listen to Mira.

19:00.514 --> 19:02.349
- I want to know the truth.
- Arisu!

19:02.432 --> 19:03.433
You really want to know?

19:07.187 --> 19:08.021
Yes.

19:13.944 --> 19:16.864
Then I guess you're prepared
to accept the truth, aren't you?

19:23.370 --> 19:24.538
All right.

19:25.873 --> 19:29.042
I'll stop prevaricating
and reveal the real truth.

19:32.212 --> 19:33.463
I'll start with the reality.

19:34.548 --> 19:37.509
The world you can see now

19:38.552 --> 19:39.720
is not real.

19:40.721 --> 19:41.805
It's an illusion.

19:46.935 --> 19:49.104
You're saying this is all an illusion?

19:49.730 --> 19:53.317
Since you've been here, didn't you doubt
even just once that it was real?

19:54.151 --> 19:55.652
The desolate city,

19:55.736 --> 19:58.947
radical technology, and ludicrous games.

19:59.031 --> 20:00.490
Is it aliens? People from the future?

20:00.574 --> 20:02.701
Even if they were behind it all,

20:02.784 --> 20:06.538
can you think of any serious reason
why they'd run these games?

20:09.291 --> 20:13.420
Tag and hide-and-seek are
both children's ideas.

20:13.962 --> 20:17.633
Nothing can happen here
that is beyond your own imagination.

20:25.807 --> 20:30.979
It's only natural that a person
like yourself would survive until now.

20:33.273 --> 20:34.691
You see, that's because…

20:36.485 --> 20:38.737
these things are happening in a tiny world

20:39.404 --> 20:44.409
that exists inside
the mere 1,500 grams of your own brain.

21:02.928 --> 21:05.847
Arisu, don't pay attention to her.

21:07.224 --> 21:08.892
If this were an illusion,

21:09.559 --> 21:13.105
then it means you believe that
my life is something you imagined!

21:13.689 --> 21:15.232
But I'm right here, alive!

21:15.315 --> 21:16.441
That's right.

21:18.402 --> 21:20.821
You do exist.

21:21.488 --> 21:26.618
But that is not the reality
that Arisu sees.

21:27.119 --> 21:28.161
What?

21:30.789 --> 21:31.623
Arisu.

21:33.792 --> 21:35.294
Don't you remember

21:36.712 --> 21:38.213
what happened then?

21:42.551 --> 21:43.552
When you lost

21:45.387 --> 21:47.723
your precious friends.

21:49.474 --> 21:53.061
The shock was so traumatic,
you lost all memory of what happened.

21:57.899 --> 21:58.942
I am

22:00.819 --> 22:06.241
your doctor, Mira Kano, a psychiatrist.

22:07.993 --> 22:11.997
You are receiving counseling from me.

22:15.250 --> 22:16.418
You simply

22:17.711 --> 22:19.379
don't remember it.

22:21.798 --> 22:23.175
You just don't remember.

22:29.931 --> 22:30.849
So…

22:33.226 --> 22:34.561
Do you remember now?

22:36.646 --> 22:38.482
Are your memories

22:40.484 --> 22:41.818
gradually returning?

23:34.704 --> 23:36.873
How about it, Arisu?

23:39.501 --> 23:43.004
Are your memories gradually returning?

23:48.593 --> 23:49.678
Chota…

23:51.555 --> 23:52.639
Karube…

24:03.733 --> 24:05.819
You two sure are close.

24:07.571 --> 24:09.072
She's always

24:10.740 --> 24:12.826
worried about you.

24:17.164 --> 24:20.917
She also lost someone precious to her

24:21.751 --> 24:23.503
and has been hospitalized here.

24:31.386 --> 24:32.304
Okay now.

24:33.138 --> 24:34.639
Tell me.

24:37.684 --> 24:39.603
Tell me what really happened

24:41.229 --> 24:43.899
when you saw those fireworks.

24:51.156 --> 24:52.157
Okay.

24:53.575 --> 24:54.743
Try to remember.

24:59.706 --> 25:00.790
At that time…

25:06.129 --> 25:08.381
- Hey!
- Oh, shit!

25:10.675 --> 25:13.136
- Yikes!
- That was close!

25:13.637 --> 25:15.555
- Hurry up!
- Look, fireworks!

25:16.139 --> 25:17.098
Run for your lives!

25:53.677 --> 25:54.928
It was my fault…

25:56.888 --> 25:57.973
that they died.

26:00.058 --> 26:01.810
You remember it all now, don't you?

26:06.898 --> 26:08.650
The one who killed them

26:09.985 --> 26:10.986
was me.

26:12.904 --> 26:14.739
What you wanted to know

26:16.324 --> 26:20.078
wasn't why this world exists.

26:21.997 --> 26:23.832
What you wanted to know was

26:26.001 --> 26:28.003
what you are.

26:29.838 --> 26:32.007
You want the answer

26:34.175 --> 26:35.510
to why you live.

26:36.386 --> 26:38.388
You want to know why you exist.

26:41.933 --> 26:44.352
You grew up starving for love.

26:46.563 --> 26:48.898
Long before you came here,

26:50.984 --> 26:53.069
you've been looking for that answer.

26:57.115 --> 26:58.116
That's why,

26:59.951 --> 27:01.536
in your fantasies,

27:02.746 --> 27:07.083
these ludicrous games appeared.

27:15.258 --> 27:17.510
As you continued to survive these games,

27:18.595 --> 27:23.433
your desire to know what this place is

27:24.434 --> 27:27.854
and your desire to know why you exist

27:29.022 --> 27:30.940
eventually became intertwined.

27:35.653 --> 27:36.988
Does anyone

27:39.032 --> 27:40.950
in this world

27:42.327 --> 27:43.912
need you?

27:47.791 --> 27:48.750
You think I can?

27:49.834 --> 27:52.003
Come now. You're fully prepared, right?

27:52.087 --> 27:53.630
I am, but…

27:57.717 --> 28:02.305
Does your existence in this world

28:03.223 --> 28:04.307
have any meaning?

28:19.364 --> 28:21.616
What's your purpose in life?

28:27.997 --> 28:30.333
How long are you
going to keep living this way?

28:35.755 --> 28:36.673
Listen.

28:39.217 --> 28:40.885
Is there a point in you being alive?

28:44.347 --> 28:45.557
But now,

28:46.391 --> 28:48.643
you're the one who survived.

28:55.734 --> 28:56.818
My life is…

28:59.070 --> 29:00.488
utterly pointless.

29:05.285 --> 29:09.748
Those guys are the ones
who should have survived.

29:13.960 --> 29:14.961
Karube…

29:16.588 --> 29:17.589
Chota…

29:22.010 --> 29:23.011
But instead,

29:24.763 --> 29:27.307
it was me, whose life
is pointless, who survived.

29:35.607 --> 29:37.442
I shouldn't be alive.

29:45.867 --> 29:46.868
Arisu…

29:47.368 --> 29:49.454
You wait outside.

29:50.330 --> 29:51.790
I haven't called you yet.

29:53.958 --> 29:54.793
Arisu!

29:54.876 --> 29:55.710
Leave him be!

29:56.544 --> 30:00.173
He's trying to remember everything now.

30:01.758 --> 30:04.385
Listen! Listen to me! Wake up!

30:04.469 --> 30:05.637
Stop it!

30:08.640 --> 30:13.311
Arisu is trying
to remember his past and recover,

30:13.394 --> 30:15.647
but you're preventing that.

30:16.856 --> 30:18.525
- You're wrong!
- Get out.

30:23.321 --> 30:24.322
Now then…

30:25.698 --> 30:26.616
Arisu.

30:30.119 --> 30:31.788
Let's bring this to an end.

30:34.123 --> 30:37.293
If I can confirm your desire to quit,

30:39.963 --> 30:41.464
the game will end.

30:45.176 --> 30:47.679
The game will end?

30:54.644 --> 30:56.145
I knew it. That wasn't…

30:57.689 --> 30:59.107
an illusion.

31:07.323 --> 31:09.492
I was participating in that game too.

31:31.055 --> 31:32.140
Okay, now.

31:32.765 --> 31:33.766
Arisu.

31:37.395 --> 31:39.689
Let me confirm it with you.

31:41.941 --> 31:43.192
You will…

31:45.320 --> 31:47.071
quit the game, right?

32:09.552 --> 32:12.138
You'll feel better
if you take this medicine.

32:15.058 --> 32:16.142
Take it.

32:23.983 --> 32:25.068
Then…

32:26.653 --> 32:27.904
give me your answer.

32:46.965 --> 32:48.716
Arisu… don't!

32:51.010 --> 32:52.762
Arisu! Don't!

33:09.278 --> 33:10.363
Put that down.

33:16.995 --> 33:18.246
Arisu…

33:23.001 --> 33:24.168
Remember what you said?

33:26.921 --> 33:29.173
You said you'd risk your life to save me.

33:34.387 --> 33:35.888
No matter what Mira says,

33:37.306 --> 33:39.225
I am most definitely here with you!

33:41.769 --> 33:42.854
I am alive!

33:47.900 --> 33:50.319
If you still believe what Mira says,

33:55.116 --> 33:56.951
then our time together will be…

34:00.121 --> 34:02.623
nothing more than an illusion you created.

34:08.546 --> 34:10.214
If it was all just an illusion,

34:14.343 --> 34:19.766
then no matter what I do,
it shouldn't affect you, right?

34:28.775 --> 34:29.650
Arisu…

34:31.903 --> 34:33.154
Wake up.

36:17.592 --> 36:18.593
Arisu…

36:20.219 --> 36:21.304
Arisu…

36:31.355 --> 36:32.440
Arisu…

36:34.192 --> 36:35.443
Wake up.

36:38.863 --> 36:39.864
Please!

36:45.703 --> 36:48.289
What a beautiful sight.

36:49.874 --> 36:50.791
But…

36:52.668 --> 36:55.254
a person's love is ultimately powerless.

37:01.928 --> 37:02.970
Arisu…

37:06.224 --> 37:07.266
Please…

37:09.810 --> 37:10.895
I…

37:12.521 --> 37:14.357
shouldn't be alive.

37:15.650 --> 37:17.652
I have no reason to live.

37:29.830 --> 37:31.249
Come back…

37:34.460 --> 37:35.544
Arisu!

37:46.931 --> 37:48.432
The answer…

37:51.310 --> 37:53.062
The reason for living…

37:56.732 --> 38:00.152
Forget about those things, Arisu.

38:06.659 --> 38:07.743
The answer

38:08.953 --> 38:10.705
is different for everyone.

38:13.541 --> 38:15.293
A reason for living…

38:17.545 --> 38:21.382
It doesn't matter if you have one or not.

38:26.512 --> 38:28.180
This whole time we've searched…

38:32.184 --> 38:34.186
we've been searching together.

38:41.152 --> 38:43.070
That alone was enough.

38:45.156 --> 38:46.407
That alone…

38:54.874 --> 38:58.044
The one who made me realize that…

39:03.716 --> 39:04.800
was you.

39:08.429 --> 39:10.014
It was you, Arisu.

39:46.842 --> 39:49.762
You poor thing.

39:55.726 --> 39:57.978
Looks like I've won.

40:05.903 --> 40:07.655
You'll quit the game,

40:09.448 --> 40:11.033
won't you, Arisu?

40:25.339 --> 40:26.257
Then…

40:29.176 --> 40:31.011
the game is over.

41:17.516 --> 41:18.434
Usagi…

41:27.067 --> 41:28.068
Usagi…

41:30.279 --> 41:32.281
I want to

41:34.617 --> 41:36.118
hold your hand again.

41:41.999 --> 41:43.918
I want to

41:45.544 --> 41:46.629
walk with you again.

41:53.135 --> 41:54.887
I want to eat with you.

42:01.435 --> 42:02.770
Me too.

42:14.782 --> 42:16.116
I want to

42:21.580 --> 42:22.748
say, "Good morning"

42:24.917 --> 42:27.878
to you again tomorrow, Arisu.

42:31.799 --> 42:34.218
I want to laugh with you every day.

42:36.804 --> 42:38.097
Just once,

42:41.892 --> 42:44.228
I'd like us to climb a mountain together.

42:46.146 --> 42:47.648
Just being with you

42:49.984 --> 42:51.902
is enough, Usagi.

42:55.531 --> 42:56.615
And even

42:59.577 --> 43:02.496
arguing sometimes would be nice.

43:07.585 --> 43:08.836
I simply want you

43:12.047 --> 43:13.382
to live, Usagi.

43:31.859 --> 43:33.861
I want to protect you, Usagi.

43:53.464 --> 43:54.632
Let's continue

43:57.801 --> 43:58.802
the game.

44:49.645 --> 44:50.646
Arisu…

44:53.273 --> 44:54.358
It's all right now.

45:07.621 --> 45:08.539
Use this.

45:20.384 --> 45:22.219
How magnificent.

45:28.350 --> 45:29.768
That was moving.

45:36.483 --> 45:38.152
For her sake as well,

45:40.779 --> 45:42.364
let's finish this game.

46:15.772 --> 46:16.690
Yes!

46:31.872 --> 46:32.789
Okay!

46:39.671 --> 46:40.547
Yes!

47:25.217 --> 47:26.218
Yes!

47:27.553 --> 47:28.971
I won!

47:47.948 --> 47:49.116
You played

47:50.617 --> 47:52.452
three rounds

47:54.121 --> 47:56.623
without quitting the game.

48:01.253 --> 48:03.422
Congratulations, Arisu.

48:05.841 --> 48:08.135
The game has ended.

48:12.973 --> 48:14.099
At last.

48:17.185 --> 48:18.270
Is it over?

48:26.278 --> 48:27.195
Yeah.

48:29.656 --> 48:30.907
We won.

48:48.634 --> 48:49.551
So…

48:50.886 --> 48:53.889
What is this place anyway?

48:59.019 --> 49:00.103
Arisu…

49:02.898 --> 49:04.566
You'll soon find out.

49:10.822 --> 49:12.824
Of your two choices,

49:14.785 --> 49:16.453
no matter which you choose,

49:18.121 --> 49:19.539
you'll know the answer.

49:21.958 --> 49:24.628
You'll know what kind of person you are.

49:26.963 --> 49:28.215
You'll know.

49:31.718 --> 49:32.969
Life is

49:34.846 --> 49:36.515
like a game.

49:39.935 --> 49:41.520
Enjoy it more.

50:12.217 --> 50:13.885
Congratulations.

50:14.594 --> 50:19.349
All the games have now been cleared.

51:29.544 --> 51:35.801
Now, all the surviving players
will be given a choice.

51:36.510 --> 51:40.263
Please select whether you will accept
permanent residence in this land

51:40.347 --> 51:42.682
or if you will not accept it.

51:44.976 --> 51:46.311
I repeat,

51:47.145 --> 51:50.816
please select whether you will accept
permanent residence in this land

51:50.899 --> 51:53.318
or if you will not accept it.

51:59.950 --> 52:01.034
I don't want it.

52:33.441 --> 52:34.359
I…

52:36.027 --> 52:37.195
don't want it!

53:04.347 --> 53:05.849
I don't want it.

53:28.747 --> 53:31.416
Let's go back together.

53:34.127 --> 53:39.382
PERMANENT RESIDENCE IN THIS LAND
ACCEPT. / DO NOT ACCEPT.

53:44.262 --> 53:46.514
Of course, I'll take it.

53:47.557 --> 53:49.476
I will gladly take it as well.

53:57.359 --> 53:58.443
I…

54:00.111 --> 54:02.864
don't want it, I think.

54:06.868 --> 54:08.453
What will you do?

54:18.004 --> 54:19.339
I don't want it.

54:51.871 --> 54:52.872
I…

54:56.126 --> 54:58.128
don't want permanent residence.

55:02.716 --> 55:03.717
I also…

55:07.804 --> 55:08.972
don't want it.

55:27.782 --> 55:28.742
The usual?

55:31.995 --> 55:32.829
Yeah.

55:33.997 --> 55:34.831
Here.

55:38.585 --> 55:39.586
What?

55:42.297 --> 55:43.298
What?

55:46.760 --> 55:48.261
Your nose hair is sticking out.

55:48.344 --> 55:49.179
No way.

55:49.971 --> 55:50.805
Seriously?

55:51.514 --> 55:52.515
Just kidding.

55:52.599 --> 55:54.267
You jerk! Cut it out!

55:59.856 --> 56:01.357
You looked so depressed.

56:02.734 --> 56:06.071
Hey, you know how you can put wax
on your nose hairs to remove them?

56:06.154 --> 56:07.822
That must really hurt!

56:07.906 --> 56:09.115
And they'll never come back?

56:09.199 --> 56:10.909
Of course, they will.

56:10.992 --> 56:13.078
A nose-hair cutter would be better.

56:13.161 --> 56:17.165
But if something fell on your head
while doing that, it'd really hurt!

56:17.248 --> 56:19.125
No. An explosion hurts more.

56:19.626 --> 56:20.668
- It sure does.
- For sure.

56:27.425 --> 56:28.426
I'm sorry.

56:30.553 --> 56:31.513
I'm sorry.

56:33.264 --> 56:34.432
It's all my fault.

56:36.351 --> 56:37.227
I'm sorry.

56:38.478 --> 56:40.396
"His fault," he says.

56:41.064 --> 56:43.066
You're as overconfident as ever.

56:43.149 --> 56:47.362
I bet you think you're alive because
you're special and a chosen one, right?

56:47.445 --> 56:48.404
No, I don't.

56:48.905 --> 56:50.323
It's all thanks to you guys.

56:50.406 --> 56:55.120
It sounds like he believes
we sacrificed ourselves so he could live.

56:55.203 --> 56:58.289
Dang, Chota.
That's a pretty cruel thing to say.

56:58.373 --> 57:00.708
Can't you see?
Arisu doesn't get it at all.

57:02.418 --> 57:03.670
What's with you guys?

57:04.963 --> 57:06.381
What are you trying to say?

57:07.882 --> 57:09.217
Make yourselves clear!

57:12.470 --> 57:14.139
One thing I can say for sure is…

57:16.266 --> 57:21.646
there wasn't a single game
that you cleared by your own effort alone.

57:22.230 --> 57:26.359
If you thanked us forever,
it would never be enough.

57:27.193 --> 57:28.111
Then…

57:29.446 --> 57:31.698
should I apologize
for the rest of my life?

57:34.367 --> 57:35.285
Don't be stupid.

57:36.119 --> 57:40.707
Live your life to the fullest
until the very end.

57:46.421 --> 57:47.338
Okay.

57:49.090 --> 57:50.008
I will.

58:34.594 --> 58:37.138
It would be bad if zombies
were to appear in Shibuya, huh?

58:37.222 --> 58:40.099
If they're all bitten here,
they will all turn into zombies!

58:40.183 --> 58:42.810
Stop it with the zombie talk,
and think about which shop to go to.

58:42.894 --> 58:45.772
But if zombies were to appear,
I guess only Karube would survive.

58:45.855 --> 58:47.607
You'd knock those zombies out
with one punch.

58:48.608 --> 58:49.943
No, it wouldn't be me.

58:50.026 --> 58:51.861
You'd be the one to survive, Arisu.

58:51.945 --> 58:53.446
Me? Why?

58:54.364 --> 58:55.949
I'm sure you're the one who will survive.

58:59.452 --> 59:00.453
All right.

59:01.037 --> 59:01.955
Here we go.

59:02.956 --> 59:04.374
- What are you doing?
- Hey!

59:04.457 --> 59:06.376
This is your Independence Day!

59:06.459 --> 59:07.627
Passing through!

59:09.212 --> 59:10.046
Move aside!

59:10.129 --> 59:12.632
- Move aside!
- Hey, this is dangerous!

59:52.213 --> 59:53.256
- Hey!
- Oh, shit!

59:55.508 --> 59:58.761
- Hurry up!
- Look, fireworks!

01:00:04.434 --> 01:00:06.394
It's the police! This is bad!

01:00:06.477 --> 01:00:07.312
Let's run for it!

01:00:11.691 --> 01:00:12.692
Over there!

01:01:54.627 --> 01:01:55.837
Can you hear me?

01:01:56.421 --> 01:01:58.172
- Can you hear me?
- Can you hear me?

01:01:58.256 --> 01:01:59.674
- Check this one.
- Got it.

01:02:01.050 --> 01:02:02.510
Checking for carotid pulse.

01:02:03.720 --> 01:02:04.637
He's breathing!

01:02:05.680 --> 01:02:07.682
He's conscious! Stretcher!

01:02:07.765 --> 01:02:09.767
- His heart's started!
- Right!

01:02:09.851 --> 01:02:12.311
Stretcher, over here! Hurry!

01:02:47.597 --> 01:02:50.475
A meteorite has exploded over Tokyo,

01:02:50.558 --> 01:02:53.895
causing severe devastation
in and around Shibuya City.

01:02:53.978 --> 01:02:56.230
Firefighting has been proceeding slowly.

01:02:56.314 --> 01:03:02.153
The identified victims are:
Kodai Tatta, Saori Shibuki,

01:03:02.904 --> 01:03:06.240
Takeru Danma, Sho Okada,

01:03:07.116 --> 01:03:10.953
Daikichi Karube, Urumi Akamaki,

01:03:11.579 --> 01:03:15.166
Momoka Inoue, Asahi Kujyo,

01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:17.335
Chota Segawa…

01:03:20.046 --> 01:03:22.048
Both Karube and Chota died.

01:03:24.258 --> 01:03:25.468
How come only I survived?

01:03:27.637 --> 01:03:28.930
Don't think about it.

01:03:30.348 --> 01:03:31.933
It'll only make you feel worse.

01:03:36.062 --> 01:03:39.607
That kind of thing
is called "survivor's guilt."

01:03:41.609 --> 01:03:43.277
"How come only I survived?"

01:03:45.029 --> 01:03:47.657
"How come they couldn't be saved?"

01:03:49.742 --> 01:03:52.495
People who survive disasters and accidents

01:03:53.287 --> 01:03:55.456
often blame themselves like that.

01:03:59.460 --> 01:04:01.712
But when the first responders found you,

01:04:02.797 --> 01:04:04.966
your heart apparently had stopped.

01:04:09.262 --> 01:04:10.429
And for a whole minute.

01:04:14.892 --> 01:04:16.269
For a whole minute,

01:04:16.769 --> 01:04:18.521
you were at the border
between life and death.

01:04:21.023 --> 01:04:22.024
One minute?

01:04:23.192 --> 01:04:24.110
Yeah.

01:04:31.534 --> 01:04:32.785
One minute, huh?

01:04:37.415 --> 01:04:38.583
It seemed

01:04:40.960 --> 01:04:42.044
more like

01:04:44.213 --> 01:04:45.548
I was

01:04:47.800 --> 01:04:50.636
in a faraway place for a very long time.

01:04:57.435 --> 01:04:58.352
Dad…

01:04:59.812 --> 01:05:00.730
He cried.

01:05:03.274 --> 01:05:04.775
The last time he cried

01:05:05.985 --> 01:05:07.570
was when Mom died.

01:05:43.564 --> 01:05:44.649
Can I help you?

01:05:47.276 --> 01:05:50.279
Apparently, your heart stopped as well.

01:05:53.032 --> 01:05:54.617
How do you know that?

01:05:58.245 --> 01:05:59.330
It happened to me too.

01:06:02.375 --> 01:06:03.417
What a coincidence.

01:06:07.129 --> 01:06:08.339
Since you almost died,

01:06:10.299 --> 01:06:11.801
did anything change with you?

01:06:14.512 --> 01:06:15.596
I'm not so sure.

01:06:17.223 --> 01:06:19.308
Well, I guess I look flashier than before.

01:06:20.810 --> 01:06:21.852
What about you?

01:06:26.190 --> 01:06:28.776
Since I've wasted my life until now,

01:06:30.403 --> 01:06:34.824
I think I'll be able to live
a more useful life from now on.

01:06:37.827 --> 01:06:39.161
That's about all.

01:06:42.707 --> 01:06:45.793
So, you were
a good-for-nothing jerk too, huh?

01:06:47.670 --> 01:06:48.587
Yeah.

01:06:56.262 --> 01:06:59.682
- Doctor, please check this exam data.
- Okay.

01:07:06.313 --> 01:07:09.900
He's come pretty far
for having survived a cardiac arrest.

01:07:10.484 --> 01:07:12.069
- Bring me some gauze.
- Okay.

01:07:19.910 --> 01:07:21.162
Are you a friend?

01:07:21.787 --> 01:07:23.372
Well… No.

01:07:28.627 --> 01:07:32.381
He's doing his best to survive too, huh?

01:07:34.216 --> 01:07:35.384
Yes, he is.

01:07:56.072 --> 01:07:57.782
Starting CPR.

01:07:57.865 --> 01:07:59.909
- Prep defib, now!
- Right!

01:07:59.992 --> 01:08:02.078
Ann! Ann Rizuna, can you hear me?

01:08:02.161 --> 01:08:03.079
Ann!

01:08:03.162 --> 01:08:03.996
Clear!

01:08:05.289 --> 01:08:07.833
- No heartbeat!
- One more time! Charge it up!

01:08:07.917 --> 01:08:10.836
- Right! Charge complete!
- Clear!

01:08:14.006 --> 01:08:15.508
Her heartbeat's back!

01:08:15.591 --> 01:08:18.344
Sinus rhythm.
BP is steady between 80 and 90.

01:08:18.928 --> 01:08:20.513
She's back. Restarting surgery.

01:08:21.097 --> 01:08:21.931
Pean clamp.

01:08:33.192 --> 01:08:34.443
Are you all right?

01:08:34.944 --> 01:08:35.778
Yes.

01:08:36.654 --> 01:08:38.155
There's no need to rush things.

01:08:39.156 --> 01:08:39.990
Okay.

01:09:28.289 --> 01:09:29.456
Welcome back.

01:09:51.228 --> 01:09:52.229
Hikari.

01:10:16.086 --> 01:10:19.089
…and has approved two trillion yen
of national treasury disbursement.

01:10:20.799 --> 01:10:26.388
It's been a week since a meteorite
exploded over Tokyo, and as of today,

01:10:26.472 --> 01:10:30.142
many sections of the railway service
are still suspended,

01:10:30.226 --> 01:10:33.812
and major highways are still closed.

01:11:11.976 --> 01:11:13.060
Excuse me…

01:11:13.894 --> 01:11:15.562
Can I use it now?

01:11:16.188 --> 01:11:18.190
Oh, sorry. Go ahead.

01:11:45.801 --> 01:11:46.719
Wait.

01:11:48.053 --> 01:11:48.971
Your change.

01:11:53.642 --> 01:11:54.643
Thank you.

01:12:07.531 --> 01:12:11.243
Sorry… Have we met somewhere?

01:12:13.787 --> 01:12:14.747
I don't think so.

01:12:19.418 --> 01:12:20.336
Wait.

01:12:25.174 --> 01:12:27.176
Are you sure we've never met before?

01:12:28.635 --> 01:12:29.470
What?

01:12:34.641 --> 01:12:36.060
Are you

01:12:37.144 --> 01:12:38.479
hitting on me?

01:12:39.313 --> 01:12:42.316
No. I'm not doing that.

01:12:45.361 --> 01:12:46.862
Well… Then…

01:12:47.529 --> 01:12:52.201
would it be all right
if I was hitting on you?

01:13:01.835 --> 01:13:02.753
Sorry.

01:13:03.629 --> 01:13:05.214
That was a weird thing to say.

01:13:10.052 --> 01:13:13.138
I think we may have met before.

01:13:17.101 --> 01:13:18.018
Last year?

01:13:18.560 --> 01:13:20.312
Two years ago?

01:13:21.021 --> 01:13:22.356
When was it?

01:13:24.608 --> 01:13:25.859
I forgot,

01:13:26.985 --> 01:13:28.570
but I think we did somewhere.

01:13:38.497 --> 01:13:40.749
Say, the weather's nice.

01:13:42.584 --> 01:13:46.088
How about taking a walk out in the garden?

01:13:48.674 --> 01:13:49.508
Sure.

01:15:01.413 --> 01:15:02.372
Wait up!

01:18:30.706 --> 01:18:35.711
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
